{"diagnosis":"CDP SystemInfo.getProcessInfo returns the process list under the nested 'info' field (info.info.processList), not info.processList. The code reads processList from the top-level response, which is undefined, so .filter throws. Fix: read info.info.processList, guard with Array.isArray, validate the browser PID as a positive number, persist the raw process info to cdp-process-info.json in the evidence directory before detaching, and detach in a finally block before any validation exception propagates. Classification remains BLOCKED_DRIVER since this is a driver/schema defect, not product failure.","old":"const info = await cdp.send('SystemInfo.getProcessInfo');
    const browserProcs = info.processList.filter(p => p.type === 'browser');
    if (browserProcs.length !== 1) throw { classify: 'BLOCKED', msg: 'browser pid ambiguous' };
    const browserPid = browserProcs[0].id;
    await cdp.detach();","new":"const resp = await cdp.send('SystemInfo.getProcessInfo');
    const processList = resp && resp.info && Array.isArray(resp.info.processList) ? resp.info.processList : null;
    if (!processList) {
      await cdp.detach();
      throw { classify: 'BLOCKED_DRIVER', msg: 'SystemInfo.getProcessInfo: missing or invalid info.processList' };
    }
    try {
      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(out, 'cdp-process-info.json'), JSON.stringify(resp.info, null, 2));
    } catch (e) { /* evidence write failure must not mask pid validation */ }
    const browserProcs = processList.filter(p => p.type === 'browser');
    const browserPid = browserProcs.length === 1 ? browserProcs[0].id : null;
    if (typeof browserPid !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(browserPid) || browserPid <= 0) {
      await cdp.detach();
      throw { classify: 'BLOCKED_DRIVER', msg: 'browser pid ambiguous or invalid: ' + JSON.stringify(browserProcs.map(p => p.id)) };
    }
    await cdp.detach();","reason":"CDP nests the payload under resp.info; resp.processList is undefined. Guarding with Array.isArray and validating the PID as a positive finite number rejects malformed/ambiguous responses, detaches before throwing (with BLOCKED_DRIVER classification), and saves the dedicated browser's raw process info as evidence without touching product code.","classification":"BLOCKED_DRIVER"}

